  Normally, you would use a connective, like  "la djan .e la djim dunda lo
djine la meris" (John and Jim gave a ring to Mary, which would mean they
each gave her a ring) or "a djan jo'u la djim dunda lo djine la meris"
(John along with Jim gave a ring to Mary).  In these cases, the x1 is the
whole connected give "John and Jim", "John along with Jim")

              --gejyspa

